// 5.64 / B6 -- all pipes below threshold: the steady network's whole-network
// dead fixed point (docs/gap_analysis.md B6, §5.49 边界⑧).
//
// Every pipe has dp < dpStatic = 4 tau0 L / d, so every Q is exactly 0 and each
// free node's balance is 0 = 0 whatever its pressure. The kernel initialises a
// free node to the MEAN of the fixed pressures (network.cpp:538-547) and evaluates
// the residual before entering Newton; here that residual is exactly zero, so the
// solve reports iterations = 0, residual = 0, converged. A dead branch gets the
// Hagen-Poiseuille conductance cap (network.cpp:519), so the Jacobian's free-node
// row is NOT singular -- it simply is never asked to invert. The checker's source
// arm proves the other half: with an injected rate the loop does run (19 steps)
// and converges, so the matrix really is invertible.
//
// Topology: 2 fixed-pressure nodes (A 3e4, B 2e4, dp = 1e4 Pa) + one free node E
// (initialised to 2.5e4 = mean of A and B). Five Bingham pipes:
//
//   pipe  from  to    tau0   threshold 4 tau0 L/d   dp offered   stuck?
//   Stk1   A    B     3.0        12000 Pa            10000 Pa      yes (dp < threshold)
//   Stk2   A    B     4.0        16000 Pa            10000 Pa      yes
//   Stk3   A    B     5.0        20000 Pa            10000 Pa      yes
//   Sr1a   A    E     3.0        12000 Pa             5000 Pa      yes (series pair)
//   Sr1b   E    B     3.0        12000 Pa             5000 Pa      yes
//
// Constants: L 20, d 0.02, rho 850, mu 0.1.
//
// Arm 1 of 6; the 4-pipe topology twin is probe.dict. The other four arms are
// derived from this file in a temp dir by the checker:
//   shifted    p(A) 3.1e4 -> E = 25500 (mean, not a hardcoded 25000)
//   knifeEdge  Stk1 tau0 2.5 -> dp == dpStatic, Q still exactly 0
//   oneFlowing Stk1 tau0 2.0 -> Q = 1.37182879207e-6 (Buckingham), iterations 0
//   injected   source 1e-6 at E -> E = 33978.9475076, Sr1b dp = 13978.9475076
//              = Buckingham's inverse at that rate, Newton 19 steps
//
// verified by tests/check_steady_all_below_threshold.py (45 checks),
// ctest verify.steadyAllBelowThreshold. Zero kernel changes.

solver
{
    type steadyNetwork;
}

fluid
{
    rho 850;
    mu 0.1;
}

nodes
{
    A { pressure 3.0e4; }
    B { pressure 2.0e4; }
    E {};
}

pipes
{
    Stk1 { from A; to B; length 20; diameter 0.02; yieldStress 3.0; }
    Stk2 { from A; to B; length 20; diameter 0.02; yieldStress 4.0; }
    Stk3 { from A; to B; length 20; diameter 0.02; yieldStress 5.0; }

    Sr1a { from A; to E; length 20; diameter 0.02; yieldStress 3.0; }
    Sr1b { from E; to B; length 20; diameter 0.02; yieldStress 3.0; }
}
